    </nav>
    <div class="reading-main">
        <section class="content-panel prose">
            <h2 id="system-integrations">
                Systems and API Integration
            </h2>
            <p>
                I integrated Zendesk, our third-party help-center documentation and training platform, with internal services that provide custom role-based access. I also developed API integrations and services that connect applications and support product functionality. My broader experience includes Encompass data synchronization, enterprise API integrations, and application services built with C#/.NET.
            </p>
            <p>
                <a asp-page="/Skills/Zendesk">Explore my Zendesk integration experience</a>.
            </p>
            <p>
                I work with explicit API contracts, clear ownership, configuration, validation, and diagnostic visibility so integrations remain understandable and supportable as systems evolve.
            </p>
            <h2 id="identity">
                Identity
            </h2>
            <p>
                I wired OAuth and OpenID Connect (OIDC) into my starter application using Okta. My shared application foundations also include authentication integration, and my QA framework provides isolated OAuth/OpenID Connect validation flows using Keycloak.
            </p>
            <p>
                <a asp-page="/Skills/Okta">Explore my Okta integration experience</a>.
            </p>
            <p>
                I consider identity and application boundaries together: how applications authenticate, where responsibilities belong, and how integration behavior can be validated.
            </p>
            <h2 id="student-systems">
                Student Information Systems
            </h2>
            <p>
                I have growing experience with Student Information Systems (SIS), helping develop and support educational applications for students.
            </p>
            <p>
                As an ICS (Information Communication Services) employee of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, I have a direct assignment supporting CES (Church Education Services) services and applications. My Global Education work includes BYU-Pathway and Seminaries and Institutes.
            </p>
            <h2 id="integration-boundaries">
                Integration Boundaries
            </h2>
            <p>
                My application starters demonstrate defensive API boundaries through same-origin proxying, payload validation, upstream restrictions, header filtering, payload limits, timeouts, safe errors, and trace correlation. My QA framework adds reusable API clients, schema validation, and diagnostic capture.
            </p>
            <p>
                <a asp-page="/Skills/WebApi">API engineering</a> · <a asp-page="/Skills/Database">Data integration</a> · <a asp-page="/Experience/EmploymentAccomplishments" asp-fragment="software-delivery">Delivered integrations</a>
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
